{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"reasoning","text":"**Evaluating trade-offs in profiling**\n\nI’m looking at the trade-offs involved in increasing evidence collection, which can lead to higher compilation and measurement costs—profiling overhead is about 25-35 times higher! Plus, training data can be expensive and complexity in distributed scheduling can grow significantly. However, this effort might be worthwhile when decisions happen often or hot paths dominate. \n\nI also find the synthesis of weighted flow graphs and feature vectors interesting. Maybe I should include human-readable titles instead of internal IDs?"}}
